================================================================================
The assistants this server exposes
================================================================================

Three assistants, on three different base models. None of them has its own
weights: each is a personality and an interface over someone else's model, and
this repository contains no model files at all.

    Caracat AI is based on gpt-oss-20b by OpenAI.

        Upstream model    openai/gpt-oss-20b
        Upstream URL      https://huggingface.co/openai/gpt-oss-20b
        Upstream license  Apache License 2.0

    Caracat Code is based on Qwen3-Coder-Next by Qwen.

        Upstream model    Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next
        Upstream URL      https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next
        Upstream license  Apache License 2.0

    Caracat Pro is based on DeepSeek-V3.1 by DeepSeek.

        Upstream model    deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3.1
        Upstream URL      https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3.1
        Upstream license  MIT License

No name may be used for another, and none may be attributed to another's
creator. The Apache-2.0 and MIT licences are not interchangeable and are not
described as one thing -- see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

Every answer these tools return carries its assistant's attribution with it.
That is deliberate: a tool has no header to put it in, and an answer passed on
through two more systems would otherwise arrive with no trace of whose model
produced it.

================================================================================
The personalities
================================================================================

The three system prompts are not stored in this repository. They are fetched at
build time from prompts/ in the model repository, so that each has exactly one
source:

    https://github.com/Pheonix-Studio-cat/training-and-devoloping-caracat-code

